WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.196
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Wait for it.

00:00:02.196 --> 00:00:04.980
[DEEP SOUND]

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.810
Well, I knew that
was going to happen.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.510
But in real life, we
rarely get advance notice

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.040
for a disruptive event.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.590
Stay tuned as we discuss how
to build a solid business

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:15.570
continuity plan.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.030
I'm Priyanka, and
welcome to Anthos 101.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.640
Many of you might have
backup and disaster recovery

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.690
plans in place.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.630
But we rarely get notified
that a disruptive event

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.860
might happen.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.160
Even with some lead time, things
can still go wrong and impact

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.660
business continuity.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.270
Let's answer seven
key questions that

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.730
can help you go beyond
traditional backup and DR.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.410
Question number 1.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.210
Are your applications
architected

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.770
for high availability
and data redundancy?

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.580
Anthos GKE helps you architect
for high availability and data

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.820
redundancy by offering
two types of clusters,

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.870
zonal and regional.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.250
In a zonal cluster topology,
a cluster's control

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.000
plane and nodes all run
in a single compute zone

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.060
that you specify when
you create the cluster.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.520
In a regional cluster,
masters and nodes

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:16.660
are replicated across multiple
zones within a single region.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.200
Regional clusters consist
of three masters, quorum,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.290
offering higher availability
than a zonal cluster.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:26.710
You can minimize the risk of
disruption to your services,

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:29.290
as well as expedite
the upgrade process

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.360
through unique features like
surge upgrades and release

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.310
channels.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.590
Anthos also enables
data protection

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:39.490
through disk snapshots stored in
any regional or multi regional

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.740
locations across Google Cloud.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.820
And disks can be attached to
regional clusters and fail-over

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.480
if a zone fails.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.590
You can combine these with
Anthos-enabled software

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.300
from the Google
Cloud Marketplace

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.580
to enable high
availability applications

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.540
such as [INAUDIBLE],, Word
Works Enterprise, Robbins

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.720
Storage, [INAUDIBLE] APS.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.770
Question number 2, can
your apps scale up and down

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.755
without code changes?

00:02:07.755 --> 00:02:09.850
When you work with
Anthos, you are

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.470
adopting modern Cloud native
technologies like containers,

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.400
serverless, and
service mesh that

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.760
enables micro services
based applications.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.950
These are modular
architectures that

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.380
make it easier to
upgrade and scale

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:28.080
up and down than a tightly
coupled monolithic application.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.100
Question number 3, do you
have consistent management

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.890
across on-prem and
multi-cloud environments?

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.760
We started the series by
answering the question, what

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.610
is Anthos, where we
covered how and those

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:45.900
can help you consistently secure
and operate existing apps,

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.860
develop and deploy new apps
across disparate locations,

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.590
while offering
centralized visibility

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.260
and management of resources.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.200
Question number 4, are
you finding and fixing

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.470
bugs before moving
to production?

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.110
Well, the only way
to ship bug free code

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:07.620
is by catching bugs and
fixing them before deployment.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.950
With increasing adoption
of hybrid and multi cloud,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:16.000
you need a modern CICD pipeline
to automatically build, test,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.930
and reliably deploy to
different environments.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.170
To learn more about how to
build a modern CICD pipeline

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.350
with Anthos, check out
a previous episode.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:29.340
Question number 5, have
you defined and implemented

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.530
measurable Service
Level Objectives

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.380
or SLOs for your apps?

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.920
It's crucial to define RTO and
RPO for business continuity.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.540
RTO, or Recovery Time
Objective, is the amount of time

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:46.020
an application can be
unavailable without causing

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.580
significant damage
to your business.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.030
RPO, or Recovery
Point Objective,

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.250
is the tolerance
of how much data

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.070
can be lost before critically
impacting your business.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.300
It helps to consider modernizing
your existing applications

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.370
to cloud native architecture.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:05.400
This will help you deliver
uninterrupted services

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.040
at an optimal cost.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.890
With Anthos, you can easily
set SLOs for your services

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.780
and monitor them.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:15.090
That brings me to
question number 6,

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:19.320
can you proactively mitigate
failures in your applications?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.010
Anthos dashboards
provides built in SLOs

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.300
so you can improve
the observability

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.610
and proactively
mitigate failures,

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.680
just like Google SREs.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.710
For more details, check out
how to improve observability

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:36.450
using golden signals episode
in the Anthos 101 series.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.990
Question number 7, do you have
access to skills to develop

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.980
and maintain your apps?

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.580
Now, this might sound
like a learning problem,

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.580
but having a standardized
technology platform, which

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.090
makes it easy for you to
manage existing applications

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.310
and build new ones helps.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.280
With Anthos, your teams
have access to skills

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:00.270
to develop and maintain apps,
not just in one environment,

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.120
but across multiple
environments.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.430
To summarize, here's
a checklist of how

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.730
to go beyond business
continuity with Anthos.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:12.180
Develop high availability
apps with data redundancy.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.390
Scale flexibly
without code changes.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:18.690
Find and fix bugs before
moving into production.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:22.380
Manage consistently across
on-prem and multi-cloud.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.910
Implement measurable SLOs,
including RTO and RPO values.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.640
Mitigate app
failures proactively.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.200
Gain sufficient
access to skills.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.470
Today we learned that Anthos
can help you build a next gen

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:40.190
business continuity plan beyond
traditional backup and disaster

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.780
recovery.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.360
Read beyond business
continuity white paper

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.160
linked below to learn more.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.230
And for more Anthos
content, don't

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:51.780
forget to subscribe and check
out the entire Anthos 101

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.330
playlist.

